%C A382864 T(n,k) is the number of partitions of n into k distinct parts. - _Alois P. Heinz_, Nov 11 2026
%H A382864 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A382864/b382864.txt">Rows n = 0..481, flattened</a>
%F A382864 G.f. of column k: x^(k*(k+1)/2) / Product_{j=1..k} (1-x^j).
%F A382864 T(n,k) = |A292047(n,k)| = |A292049(n,k)|.
%F A382864 From _Alois P. Heinz_, Nov 11 2026: (Start)
%F A382864 Sum_{k>=0} k * T(n,k) = A015723(n).
%F A382864 T(n*(n+1)/2,n) = 1.
